  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Banks, finance companies and customers pay for accuracy, trust and clear explanation. They judge you by integrity, error rate and how you treat people.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is checking a calculation twice before sharing it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and skills for banking and finance careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools run calculations, draft summaries and flag patterns. Routine processing shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ethics, judgment and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to calculate and check; later, own decisions and customer trust.
  </p>

